# Normalise to LF in the index and in the working tree on every platform.
# The schema-drift test compares schemas/task-state.schema.json byte-for-byte
# against freshly generated content, which always uses LF — a CRLF checkout
# would fail that test on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The Zera supervisor runs under Windows PowerShell 5.1 from a deployed copy
# that must be byte-equal to a commit (ADR 2026-10-19). Its .ps1 files carry a
# UTF-8 BOM; every byte is kept exactly as committed, never normalised.
ops/zera-supervisor/** -text
